# Goal: classify one literal IP address for a read-only network preflight.
# Input: the address includes an interface scope, `fe80::1%eth0`.
# Change: none; this is arithmetic and validation, not a network query.
# Result: a link-local address prints a reminder about interface scope;
# other classes produce no output in this minimal example.

# Role of yesh: make the read-only network check and failure path explicit; Linux networking tools provide the observation.
address = ip fe80::1%eth0

if is link-local $address:
    echo "link-local address requires an interface scope"
